window.COPY={"a2h-baptist":{"txt":"Baptist Memorial Hospital-Fayette County is a community hospital that brings emergency treatment, inpatient care and diagnostic services into one local facility. The planned program includes eight emergency beds, eight inpatient beds, telehealth, imaging and laboratory services. A2H's architecture and engineering keep the building compact, with a glass-fronted lobby and a covered emergency drop-off that connect public arrival and waiting to the clinical spaces needed for emergency care and short hospital stays.","sub":"Public and clinical spaces","det":"Interior studies of the lobby, nurse station and dining area share a related palette of materials and finishes, with wood tones, blue accents and plenty of daylight. Together they show the range of settings in the planned hospital, from patient and visitor arrival to clinical work and smaller gathering spaces. These views complement the exterior by bringing the project down to the scale of the people who will use it.","area":"18,233 SF","scope":"Proposed hospital / CON filing"},"a2h-didd":{"txt":"This regional office and support campus in Arlington serves state programs for Tennesseans with disabilities. A2H provided architecture and engineering for the $45 million West Tennessee Regional Office project. The 15-acre campus, opened in March 2026, has three buildings: administration, a seating and positioning clinic, and maintenance and warehouse. It gathers office functions and related facilities on one site, where each building has its own identity and the landscape and circulation tie them together, as the overall planning studies show. Deep roof overhangs mark the entries, and glass-lined corridors look onto shared lawns.","sub":"A campus of related facilities","det":"The overall aerial places the regional office among the campus's supporting buildings and landscape. Separate building studies develop the architectural character of each of those pieces, while the wider view shows the setting they share.","area":"15-acre campus","scope":"Floor-area total unresolved"},"a2h-covington":{"txt":"Covington's elementary and middle school campus was rebuilt after the March 2023 tornado, a major investment in the city's educational infrastructure. A2H's work with Tipton County Schools combines technology-equipped learning environments, updated safety features and shared spaces. Outside, each school has its own prominent entrance, and a steady rhythm of light and dark vertical bands across the facade gives the renewed campus a cohesive identity for students and the wider community."},"a2h-houston":{"txt":"This addition to Houston Middle School expands specialized learning and athletics while creating a secure entrance on Johnson Road. It brings together a 1,100-seat competition gymnasium, band facilities, two art rooms and three STEM classrooms. Tall gridded windows between brick piers form a glazed public frontage that gives the addition a clear identity on campus, and the interiors balance shared school life with the distinct needs of creative, technical and physical education. The addition opened in January 2023.","sub":"Spaces for making and learning","det":"Inside, each kind of specialized learning gets a room with its own identity. A high-ceiling band room has space for colorguard practice, the expanded art facilities include pottery kilns, and the STEM rooms support flexible teaching. The competition gym doubles the previous seating capacity, so the addition serves larger school gatherings as well as everyday classes.","area":"42,974 SF","scope":"Addition"},"a2h-thompson":{"txt":"The Thompson Machinery regional headquarters is a campus in Collierville that brings the main building, service facilities and rental operations into one coordinated site plan. Each building gets its own identity, yet dark metal panels, wood-toned accents and a covered front walk make them read as one family. The exterior perspectives and an aerial explain how workplace, service frontage, circulation and landscape fit together across the larger equipment campus.","sub":"Workplace within an equipment campus","det":"Seen from above and up close, the headquarters is clearly tied to the service and rental facilities around it. Differences in scale and frontage tell visitors what each building does, while the shared architectural family holds the group together. The composition also makes the site easy to read, with buildings, access routes and landscaped areas working as parts of a single working environment.","area":"174,970 SF main building","scope":"Component / design documentation"},"a2h-dresden":{"txt":"The Dresden Municipal Complex is a new home for the city's municipal services. Following the December 2021 tornado, A2H helped assess damaged city facilities and designed the replacement, which opened in May 2025. City hall, police and fire departments share one civic setting around a paved entry court, with dedicated workspaces, flexible meeting areas and a public community safe space. The complex balances each department's needs with shared facilities, and disaster recovery is central to its purpose and program.","sub":"Shared needs, distinct departments","det":"The program includes a courtroom, firefighter sleeping quarters, a police patrol room, evidence storage and records rooms. Flexible shared spaces serve several departments, while the community safe space responds directly to the disaster behind the project. Views of the courtyard, a glass-lined corridor and the apparatus bay show the different scales of this combined civic program.","area":"17,824 SF","scope":"Building"},"a2h-oosm":{"txt":"Oxford Orthopaedics & Sports Medicine is a facility organized around a tall glazed entry tower and a covered arrival. The tower gives the practice an address patients can recognize from the parking lot, and the canopy shelters them at the door. Inside, the arrival continues through reception, waiting and a feature stair, with daylight, materials and circulation used the same way from the public face down to the scale of one patient.","sub":"From arrival to the interior","det":"The feature stair climbs inside the glass tower, so the look of the entrance carries straight into the interior. Reception and waiting pick up the same emphasis on daylight and material character at a more personal scale. Together, the exterior identity of the practice and the experience of walking in and moving through it read as one idea.","area":"27,000 GSF","scope":"Archived design / 2020"},"a2h-orthosouth":{"txt":"This 26,074-square-foot outpatient surgery center and pain-management clinic is part of a wider repositioning of the Exeter medical campus in Germantown. It sits below OrthoSouth's main orthopaedic practice and extends the building's healthcare program with dedicated patient-facing and clinical spaces. A2H's architecture and interior design lead patients from a covered drop-off and glass entry into waiting, recovery and treatment areas within the existing facility.","sub":"A renewed outpatient environment","det":"Patient waiting, recovery and clinical workspaces extend the orthopaedic program inside the existing building. Wood-toned walls, a curved reception desk and easy transitions from one space to the next give patients and staff a consistent outpatient environment. The surgery center is one piece of a wider campus renovation effort spanning ten related subprojects.","area":"26,074 SF","scope":"Expanded ASC tenant space"},"a2h-marshall":{"txt":"This 8,000-square-foot health center replaces an aging county facility with examination rooms, medical offices, community space and supporting functions. The architecture pairs familiar rural building forms with contemporary materials, and a sheltered entrance under an extended roofline shows visitors where to arrive. A timber trellis shades the front walk. The project brings clinical care and community programming together in one building serving Lewisburg and Marshall County.","area":"7,995 SF","scope":"Building"},"a2h-unioncity":{"txt":"This 24,000-square-foot medical office building brings women's health and cardiology services to the Union City hospital campus. Developed with Big River Development for Baptist Medical Group, it includes a ground-floor women's health center, with Stern Cardiology occupying the remaining space. A covered entrance and a glazed corner mark the public arrival, giving patients a sheltered drop-off and giving the clinics inside a distinctive front.","sub":"A focused clinical program","det":"The 12,000-square-foot women's health center includes 18 examination rooms, two procedure rooms, two ultrasound suites, a laboratory and conference space. Being on the hospital campus places these outpatient services alongside a broader range of care. The glazed corner and the open stair inside it are developed further as part of how people arrive and move through the building.","area":"24,000 SF","scope":"Two-story building"},"a2h-olivebranch":{"txt":"This low-rise medical office building gives outpatient care in Olive Branch a clear presence of its own. Brick and dark masonry volumes, a glazed entrance and a projecting canopy shape the public front, so patients can spot the door from the parking area and be dropped off under cover. Inside, the waiting room looks back out through that same glass, and the exterior and interior studies carry one warm material palette across the public spaces."},"a2h-millington-cte":{"txt":"This career and technical education building extends the architectural identity of the Millington school campus. A long frontage and a defined corner entrance, framed in gold and carrying the school name and mascot, give the facility a recognizable public face. The project graphics and renderings explain the building's scale, materials and relationship to the surrounding campus, bringing the proposed learning environment into focus for presentations."},"a2h-milan-park":{"txt":"The McKellar Park master plan brings playgrounds, courts, a skate park and open recreation space into one connected public landscape. Looping walking routes, parking and a pavilion organize how people arrive and gather, linking activities that need very different kinds of space. The overall aerial shows how the park sits in its neighborhood, while ground-level views give a feel for the individual places for play and social use.","sub":"Places for play and gathering","det":"Ground-level views treat the playground, skate park and courts as distinct destinations within the larger plan. Different surfaces, equipment and edges give each activity its own setting, from colorful climbing mounds to concrete bowls and rails. Paths and shared open areas connect these recreation spaces, carrying the master plan from the scale of the neighborhood down to the experience of each park user.","area":"Approximately 8 acres"},"a2h-caruthersville":{"txt":"This adaptive reuse of the 1916 Exchange Building supports the revitalization of downtown Caruthersville. A2H's proposal combines events and gallery space, Chamber of Commerce offices and upper-floor uses, while addressing accessibility, code deficiencies and project phasing. Restoration and an addition turn the brick building into a renewed civic destination, linking the historic street frontage to interior gathering spaces and an outdoor edge with a patio, pergola and murals.","sub":"Historic fabric and new gathering space","det":"The renovation and addition create 8,560 square feet of programmed space. A2H also assisted with grant planning, and the first-floor uses support the arts council, public events and the Chamber of Commerce. Views of the solarium and patio, along with the planning studies, show how the public program reaches out from the historic building into places where people can gather.","area":"8,560 SF","scope":"Renovation and addition"},"a2h-southaven":{"txt":"Southaven Fire Station No. 5 gives an essential public service a distinct presence along its street. A prominent tower marked with the station number, masonry walls and layered roof forms make the building easy to recognize from the road, with the arched apparatus bay doors off to one side. The exterior study works out how those pieces meet the public approach, presenting the station as both a working facility and a recognizable civic building."},"a2h-tipton":{"txt":"The Tipton County Animal Shelter brings public reception and dedicated animal-care areas together in a single facility. Outside, gabled roofs and bright red panels point visitors to the entrance. Inside, the studies explore a daylit reception area, cat rooms and kennel areas. The selected views connect the building's civic presence with the practical spaces that support staff, animals and visitors every day."},"a2h-northdelta":{"txt":"This multipurpose building is an addition that expands the existing North Delta school facilities in Batesville. A large main volume in the school's green sits beside the football field, with a glazed entrance that gives students and visitors a clear place to arrive and ties the building back to the rest of campus. The visualizations and presentation materials were made to show its scale, its character and how it meets the athletic fields, supporting discussion of the proposed expansion."},"a2h-vumc":{"txt":"This project is a modular MRI building for Vanderbilt University Medical Center in Nashville. The building is a compact clinical box, so the design work went into the skin, giving patients a clear front door and giving a small building a presence on its site. A glass door under a suspended canopy, with the sign right beside it, tells people where to go.","sub":"Facade study","det":"Several exterior schemes were rendered from the same viewpoint so they could be compared directly. The studies test smooth panels, a gridded panel pattern with a siding band, and a brick base under light panels. One scheme wraps the building in brick with a panel cornice above. Every option keeps the same entry, a glass door under a suspended canopy with the sign beside it."},"a2h-bmg":{"txt":"The Exeter BMG imaging suite is part of the broader conversion of the former Baptist Rehab Hospital into a medical office campus. Within that larger renovation effort, the imaging project gives patients a distinct arrival, waiting and reception environment. Warm wood tones, a stone-faced reception desk and light finishes set a consistent interior character, connecting the suite's public spaces to the campus's renewed outpatient setting.","sub":"A consistent interior arrival","det":"Reception, waiting and lobby studies work out what patients see and feel when they arrive at the imaging suite. Wood surfaces draw the eye to key elements, while light finishes carry through the adjoining spaces. The sequence ties the overall interior design to smaller decisions about arrival, orientation and the character of the patient-facing rooms.","area":"4,023 SF","scope":"Tenant planning area / 2020"},"a2h-millington-mp":{"txt":"This schematic design exercise explores a multipurpose addition within an existing school campus. The proposal organizes a large shared hall with supporting rooms, including classrooms and an ROTC space, and considers how the new building connects to surrounding school facilities such as the existing gymnasium. Exterior studies and presentation plans work through the relationship between the main volume, its entrance and the campus, turning early planning decisions into an architectural direction for discussion.","area":"10,396 SF hall","scope":"Component only / schematic"},"a2h-bolivar":{"txt":"The Bolivar NeighborHub is a community workspace that brings open work areas and enclosed meeting rooms into one shared setting. Interior studies work out how collaborative space, smaller rooms and circulation fit together, using furniture, finishes and glazing to make the plan easy to read. Glass-fronted rooms and a larger room with rows of tables beside tall windows give people a range of places to work and gather within one consistent interior."},"a2h-waste":{"txt":"This office and operations project for Waste Connections in Memphis carries one architectural character through its public and staff spaces. A glazed entrance sets up the arrival, and the interior studies continue the design through the lobby, meeting and break areas. Wood feature walls set against white surfaces and exposed steel joists overhead give the workplace a practical feel, tying the administrative side to the wider operational setting."},"a2h-milanpb":{"txt":"The Milan Public Works Building is a maintenance facility that pairs a substantial working volume with a clearly defined public entrance. A strong sloping roofline and a long service frontage of glazed overhead doors express the building's working character, while glazing marks where visitors arrive. Exterior and site studies bring those pieces together, looking at both the immediate approach and the wider working site."},"a2h-soccer":{"txt":"The Milan Soccer Complex is a planning study that brings playing fields, walking routes, parking and supporting landscape into one site plan. The aerial visualization shows the scale and organization of the proposal, with an entry drive leading through trees to parking and shelters set right beside the fields. Presented at the scale of a campus, it makes clear how access and shared space serve the athletic program, with the fields as the main structure of the landscape."},"a2h-henderson":{"txt":"The new Henderson County Health Department expands space for examination, consultation, laboratory work and community education. Bringing clinical services and public learning together is meant to strengthen local access to care. A deep entry canopy and a raised band of windows above it make the front door easy to find. A2H's design work answers the county's service needs while making careful use of state and county investment in the replacement facility."},"a2h-shelby":{"txt":"The Shelby County Center for Safety & Justice is designed to support people in the justice system who face mental health challenges. A2H led the design with national and local partners, bringing evaluation, counseling, short-term stabilization and discharge planning into one coordinated program. A two-story glass entry under a floating roof gives the low masonry building an open, approachable front. The project connects immediate support with planning for continuing care beyond the facility."},"a2h-overland":{"txt":"The Memphis Overland Building is a two-story brick building at 421 Monroe Avenue in Memphis, studied here for reuse. The rendering shows the storefronts reopened with new glass and the brick and terra cotta trim cleaned, so people on the street can see into the building again. A small canopy marks the door on the corner, and tall windows on both floors bring daylight deep inside.","sub":"Facade study","det":"The storefront and window frames were tested in several colors from the same viewpoint, including white, green and dark schemes, so the owner could compare each one against the existing brick. A photograph records the building as it stood in 2020, with most of its openings closed up."},"x-blue":{"txt":"Blue Ridge is a set of exterior studies for a multi-story medical office building. A stone-clad tower marks the corner and carries the signage, while bands of glass and light panels wrap the upper floors. The studies also look at how patients arrive, with a covered drop-off at the front door, surface parking close by and a parking deck next to the building."},"a2h-anderson":{"txt":"This master plan lays out a residential development in Brownsville, Tennessee. Homes and townhouses sit around a clubhouse, pool and play areas, so neighbors can reach the shared amenities along lawns and walking paths. A small commercial corner at the entrance gives the development a face on the street, and the aerial views show sport courts and a pavilion set between the townhouse rows."},"a2h-astoria":{"txt":"Astoria Square is a mixed-use development in Millington, Tennessee, where apartments and hotel rooms sit above shops and restaurants. The buildings gather around a central green and a covered stage. The renderings look at the district from the air, from the street and from a restaurant patio, where outdoor tables face the lawn with the hotel rising beyond it."},"a2h-benson":{"txt":"Benson Martin is a residential subdivision plan, presented along with its entrance. At eye level, a brick entry sign sits in a planted island and leads onto a tree-lined street with sidewalks and lamp posts. From above, the lots and winding roads read as a whole, with homes spread across open green parcels."},"a2h-carlisle":{"txt":"This project is a new industrial facility and its site. Visitors and staff arrive at an entry marked by a blue sign canopy and a stone base, with a wide glass storefront set between them. Aerial views take in the property as a whole, showing the plant, the truck courts and the tree-lined employee parking together."},"a2h-carroll":{"txt":"This farmers market pavilion sits at the Carroll County fairgrounds in Tennessee. Open vendor bays run along its front between brick piers, and a covered hall holds long tables for market days and community events. A wood-lined ceiling follows the pitch of the roof, giving shoppers and vendors shade and shelter."},"a2h-frayser":{"txt":"Frayser-Trezevant is a new 270,000 SF community high school for 1,500 students in Memphis, bringing two existing high schools onto one campus; it is scheduled to open for the 2027-28 school year. The design development scheme centers on a learning stair, where students can sit and gather on wide wooden tiers, and it also covers the front approach, the entry plaza and the courtyard. The earlier schematic concept is included as well, with the campus seen from the air, the courtyard stair tower and the gym entry.","area":"270,000 SF"},"a2h-hardin":{"txt":"This is a correctional training facility in Hardin County, Tennessee. The long, low building has a brick base and a green metal roof, with a secure yard at one end. Wide windows face the approach, and the fenced yard gives vehicles and equipment a protected place right beside the building."},"a2h-overton":{"txt":"This small project is a seating and planter wall at the edge of new parking for the Memphis Zoo in Overton Park. The retaining wall is stepped to make a bench, a planter and a stair, so people walking in from the lot have a place to stop on the way. Light masonry, flowering beds and a handrail along the bench keep it comfortable and easy to use beneath the park's trees."},"grec-222":{"txt":"Randolph Plaza is GREC's design proposal for The John Buck Company at 222 West Randolph: a 40-story, 1,000,000 SF office tower in the Chicago Loop. At street level the glass base opens the lobby to the sidewalk, and its glowing yellow art wall can be seen from outside. Higher up, a planted sky lobby is set into the glass facade, giving people in the building a room with trees and long views over the city."},"grec-akh":{"txt":"Akhdar Green City is a master plan for a new coastal city. Neighborhoods cluster on the headland around green corridors, with a marina and waterfront district along the shore. Seen from the air, the rounded neighborhood clusters fan out from the center toward the hills behind, and waterways thread between them down to the sea."},"grec-ch":{"txt":"Chicago and Hudson is a residential tower at Chicago Avenue and Hudson in Chicago. A brick and glass base holds the street edge, with storefront glass along the sidewalk, and the apartment tower rises behind it in a lighter skin of glass and metal. The views show the building both from the sidewalk and as part of the skyline."},"grec-china":{"txt":"Zhong Shan Shun Xiang is a mixed-use development in China with office towers, retail and a hotel. Two angled glass office towers and a hotel block rise from a shared base, where the shopping centre sits under ribbons of landscaped roof. Entries, terraces and gardens are worked into that base, so people can move between the three uses without leaving the site."},"grec-golf":{"txt":"This project is a resort hotel at the Abu Dhabi golf course. Stone-clad wings step down toward terraces and pools, and winged roofs lift above the upper floors. Guests arrive under a broad stone entry canopy off a paved court."},"grec-kimp":{"txt":"These renderings for a Kimpton hotel show two of its most public moments. Inside, a warm, richly colored lobby lounge gathers sofas and bright rugs beside a wall of tall windows. Outside, the street entry sits under a glass canopy at the base of the tower, with an outdoor dining terrace that puts tables and umbrellas right along the sidewalk."},"grec-king":{"txt":"Kingsbury is a residential tower in Chicago with terrace and amenity spaces for the people who live there. The tower's brick and glass rise from a corner site, with trees and storefront glass along the sidewalk. Above the street, a landscaped terrace offers shaded tables, planting and a fountain, and a glass-walled dining room looks out over the skyline at night."},"grec-kp":{"txt":"Khalifa Park is a master plan for a 130 acre park in Abu Dhabi, organized around a central water body with gardens, plazas and pavilions along its edge. The plan drawings and a hand sketch show how visitors would move between the districts, following paths and crossings around the water from one group of pavilions and gardens to the next."},"grec-levy":{"txt":"These are club and concession interiors for the stadium in Tampa, planned around how fans spend a game day. A team-branded club lounge gives ticket holders a place to sit and eat between red draped bays, a bar keeps the game in view on large screens, and a concession stand on the concourse is signed boldly enough to find in a crowd."},"bf-4320":{"txt":"4320 West Madison turns an existing brick building in Chicago into loft apartments with a gymnasium. The apartments keep the tall ceilings, exposed brick and open ductwork of the old building, with kitchens that open onto the living rooms and large windows that fill the bedrooms with light. The gymnasium sits under white steel trusses and skylights, ringed by brick walls."},"bf-flow":{"txt":"Flow is a branded convenience store concept for Los Angeles, covering the exterior, the sales floor and the service counter. A curved gray canopy and bright green signs make the store easy to spot from the street. Inside, a green line in the floor leads shoppers past snacks, coolers and a coffee island to a glass-fronted counter for liquor and money services."},"bf-hyd":{"txt":"Hydrate is a bar interior in Chicago, kept dark so the bar itself draws people in. An island bar with a lit front sits at the center of the room, backed by a glowing bottle display. Wood floors and screens along the walls leave open space all around it, so guests can gather on every side."},"bf-lark":{"txt":"Lark is a bar and restaurant in Chicago, shown here as both an interior and a storefront. A dark paneled front with wide windows lets passersby see in from the sidewalk. Inside, a long carved wood bar runs along one wall over a herringbone floor, and a fireplace lounge with soft chairs gives guests a quieter place to settle."},"bf-nywf":{"txt":"New York Wing Factory is a restaurant and bar interior in Chicago, built for watching a game over a meal. A wood-fronted bar runs under a row of screens, with pendant bulbs and wood ceiling panels overhead. A dining room with red booths lines the brick wall opposite, where more screens keep every table in view of the action."},"bf-rav":{"txt":"Ravinia 555 is a set of apartment interiors showing an open living room and kitchen with a stone island, and a bedroom. Wood-look floors and pale cabinets keep the rooms bright, and wide windows look out to the trees. The renderings were made to let a future tenant see the finishes and the daylight before the units were built."},"bf-replay":{"txt":"Re-Play is an arcade bar in Chicago where the games share the room with the drinks. The long bar is backed by lit shelving and scoreboards on a brick wall, with arcade cabinets along the room's edge. Metal stools, hanging glass pendants and a warm glow under the bar top make it an easy place to stay between rounds."},"bf-rpa":{"txt":"Replay Andersonville is an arcade bar in Chicago's Andersonville neighborhood. A wood-clad bar sits at the center under a slatted ceiling, with rows of arcade cabinets and pinball machines along the brick walls. Seating wraps the bar on every side, so friends can watch the screens overhead or keep an eye on whose turn is next."},"kg-asc":{"txt":"The Ascension Administration Building is a new cemetery administration building and site in Libertyville, Illinois. Gabled wings with dark metal roofs step along the drive, ending in a round glazed room beneath a small cupola. Covered drop-offs at the entries give families a sheltered place to arrive, and the site views show the parking, walks and pond around it."},"kg-assum":{"txt":"The Assumption Crypt Buildings design is a crypt and columbarium building in Wheaton, Illinois, seen from outside and from within its chapel hall. A glazed gable entry sits between long walls of crypt fronts in brick and stone. Inside, the hall rises to a wood ceiling and opens to rooms of lit niches where families can visit."},"kg-cath":{"txt":"Saint Catherine is a church interior renovation paired with a new parish reception area. In the church, wood beams, white brick and stained glass windows frame the pews, and a white marble platform lifts the altar beneath the crucifix. The reception area greets visitors with a long marble desk set in front of a wood wall of carved figures."},"kg-hf":{"txt":"Holy Family is a stone chapel mausoleum and a new entrance for a cemetery. The chapel's open timber porch frames a shrine wall, with pointed arch panels set into the stone on either side. The view from the entry drive was made to show how visitors would first see the chapel across the grounds."},"kg-hnd":{"txt":"These are concept studies for a chapel in a wooded setting in McHenry County, Illinois. Three options were modeled, a round domed chapel, a columned temple and a modern pavilion, so the client could compare them on the same site. Each one is set among the same trees and lawn, which makes the differences in shape and character easy to judge."},"kg-niu":{"txt":"This project adds new dugouts and field-side improvements for the softball program at Northern Illinois University. Each dugout carries a viewing deck on its roof, so the renderings look at the field from the stands, from the bench and from above. Brick end walls, wood benches and Huskies red give players a home that matches the rest of the ballpark."},"kg-qoh":{"txt":"Queen of Heaven is a garden crypt complex at a cemetery, organized as walled courtyards around a lawn and a stained glass focal wall. The renderings follow the path from the entrance drive into the courts, where families would walk and stop. Pale stone walls, marble crypt fronts, planting beds and benches keep the courts calm and open to the sky."},"kg-sj":{"txt":"Saint Joseph is a garden crypt courtyard at a cemetery. Stone piers and a glass canopy shelter the walks between crypt walls, and a statue and fountain mark the center where visitors arrive. Benches and planting along the walks give families places to sit, with daylight coming through the canopy overhead."},"kg-sme":{"txt":"This is a garden crypt wall and shrine for Saint Mary cemetery in Elmhurst, Illinois. Brick walls of crypt fronts step out from a central gabled shrine, giving families a clear place to arrive and a place to pause. A statue stands before the arched center bay, and a paved walk with flower beds runs the length of the wall."},"kg-stmary":{"txt":"The St. Mary Administration Building is shown in exterior views and a series of interiors. Outside, low stone volumes are gathered around a taller tower topped with a cross, with stained glass set into the walls. Inside, the gathering rooms are lit by skylights and colored glass, with a few armchairs where visitors can sit and wait."},"mca-30":{"txt":"30 Court is a set of shared amenity interiors for a residential building in Morristown, New Jersey. They include a lounge built around a media wall, a dining room with a wood-beamed ceiling, and the lobby that connects them. The renderings show how residents would gather, eat and pass through the rooms, with warm wood slats and dark beams tying the spaces together."},"mca-pad":{"txt":"The Evanston Paddle Club is a clubhouse interior with a bar and a fireplace lounge. Timber trusses and a plank ceiling run over both spaces, and large windows keep the courts and trees in view. The renderings show leather chairs gathered at the fireplace, a few steps from the bar where players can meet after a match."},"mca-prin":{"txt":"These are the clubhouse interiors for a residential community. A two-story lounge gathers sofas, a billiards table and a see-through fireplace under a wood ceiling, with a quieter sitting room on the far side of the hearth and a cafe bar with a long marble-look counter. The renderings show the rooms furnished and in use so residents can picture an evening there."},"mek-as":{"txt":"This is a cemetery chapels and administration complex in Des Plaines, carried from schematic design through construction drawings. A long covered entry leads families into a lobby that links three chapels of different sizes, a meet and greet room and private family rooms beside the offices. Outside, pale block walls curve gently and tall panels of stained glass mark the chapel end."},"mek-bron":{"txt":"Bronswood is a mausoleum building set into a sloping cemetery lawn. The classical front faces the drive, with a columned porch and carved pediment under a green metal roof, and a lower level opens to the rear down a railed walk. The views show it in daylight and at dusk, so the client could see how it sits on the hill at different hours."},"mek-fr":{"txt":"These are studies for a committal shelter and an administration building at Fort Rosecrans in San Diego. The shelter gives families a covered place to gather for a service, with stacked stone piers holding a low curved metal roof over benches. The administration building uses the same stone and curved red roofs, so the buildings read as one family along the cemetery drive."},"mek-hsm":{"txt":"This is a garden mausoleum complex at Holy Sepulchre Cemetery. Crypt buildings fan out from a round central court topped by a glass skylight, with small gardens and benches between them for visitors. The views take in the approach walk through pale stone piers, the curved crypt walls and the full plan from above."},"mek-hso":{"txt":"These are garden crypt buildings at Holy Sepulcher Cemetery in Orange, California. Long terraced crypt walls step along the drive, faced in green stone and broken by stone piers. Partway along, the wall opens into a statue court with a small fountain where families can gather."},"mek-il93":{"txt":"This is a remodel of a corporate cafeteria at Motorola's Libertyville campus. The plan gives staff a branded servery, cafe counters and several kinds of seating, from window tables to lounge chairs along a curved balcony. Red stools, pale wood tabletops and a round canopy over the coffee bar make it an easy place to meet a coworker as well as eat lunch."},"mek-mill":{"txt":"These are corporate office interiors for Milestone. A double-height reception sets the tone with a red feature wall and a glass-railed balcony looking down on the desk, followed by a rounded corridor hub with a small lounge. Beyond that, a cafe and meeting space with bright mixed chairs sits beside an open stair, giving staff a casual place to get together."},"mek-oliv":{"txt":"Olivet is a mausoleum and memorial garden. The building's arched front frames a mural of a lake in autumn, with round windows above the two entry arches. In front, the garden steps down in concentric rings around a central fountain, and a pergola at the top of the slope gives visitors a shaded place to pause."},"mek-pa06":{"txt":"This is a remodel of the corporate cafeteria and servery at Motorola Mobility in Horsham. A curved white wall welcomes staff to the cafe, and the dining room opens up behind it with wood floors and tall windows. Round ceiling clouds, a teal banquette around a column and red fabric canopies near the glass break the big room into friendlier places to sit."},"mek-res":{"txt":"These are crypt and niche buildings at Resurrection Cemetery in Justice, Illinois. Low buildings wrap a curved drive and form sheltered garden courts with benches, where visitors can sit near the crypt walls. Bands of light and dark granite run across the fronts, and smaller niche walls with planters bring the scale down along the walk."},"mek-smc":{"txt":"This project converts St. Mary Church in Pittsburgh into a place of remembrance, with interior crypt walls and a memorial garden. Inside, tall wood-faced crypt walls stand free under the vaulted ceiling, leaving the brick walls and stained glass windows in view. Outside, a brick archway leads visitors from the church into a garden of lawns, paths and low crypt walls."},"mek-spp":{"txt":"This is a crypt addition at Sts. Peter and Paul Cemetery in Naperville, Illinois. Two crypt buildings in red brick and green stone flank a domed shrine with a glass roof and a cross on top. The site views show them arranged around a circular court off the cemetery drive, where families can park close by and walk straight in."},"mek-sun":{"txt":"This is a cemetery garden, pavilion and administration building at Sunset Hill in Glen Carbon. A stream runs downhill from the building through rocks and plantings, with paths on both sides and a small wood footbridge at the bottom. Up top, a terrace with a timber pergola gives families a place to stand and look out over the garden."},"str-cul":{"txt":"The Culinary Arts Lab at Rich South is a teaching kitchen with a dining lab next door. Students cook at rows of stainless steel work tables in front of a commercial cooking line, with windows along one side. The dining lab has a whiteboard wall and serving tables where they can plate and present what they made."},"str-d227":{"txt":"This is a new concession and ticket building at the stadium entry for District 227. One long white brick wall bends across the plaza and frames two gateways, marked Home and Visitors, with ticket windows between them. Past the gates, a paved court with red umbrella tables sits beside the track, so fans have a place to gather before they find a seat."},"str-oo":{"txt":"This is a 3-story renovation of Old Orchard Junior High School in Skokie, with new design elements, finishes and ceilings. The corridors get carpet with blue accents, blue lockers, wood doors and bright new ceilings, alongside brick walls and a mosaic mural. The result gives students lighter, quieter hallways without erasing the building they know."},"str-rc":{"txt":"This is a commons and cafeteria addition at Reed-Custer High School. Tall windows open the room to a covered patio with outdoor tables, and ring lights hang over round cafeteria tables inside. Wood panels and a large school mural warm up the block walls. One building model drove both the construction documents and the views shared with the client."},"sg-balt":{"txt":"The dining decks of a harbor cruise vessel are reworked here as one two-level room, with an open well between the decks. Guests at the upper rail look down on the tables below and across to a bar at each level. The renderings follow a guest from that rail down to the tables and the buffet line, with daylight coming in along both sides."},"sg-enr":{"txt":"The Enrichment Center is a learning and activity space for young people. Bench seating with turf tops, work tables and a large screen share one open room under a pitched ceiling. The renderings show pegboard walls, workbenches along the windows and a checkered floor, a room where kids can build something, watch something or just sit together."},"sg-hcal":{"txt":"This is the dining room of a harbor cruise vessel in California, with a long bar, banquet seating and a dance floor under a raised ceiling. High windows in the raised section bring daylight down to the dance floor and a grand piano beside it. The renderings show the room set for an evening sailing, with city lights in the windows."},"sg-hent":{"txt":"This is the dining deck of a harbor cruise vessel, with banquet seating, a bar and a buffet wall. Windows run the length of both sides, so nearly every table has a view of the water. The renderings show the room set for dinner with the skyline through the windows."},"sg-lady":{"txt":"This is the dining salon of a charter yacht, planned around a bar, long banquet tables and window seating. The renderings show the room set for a private event, with wood plank floors underfoot, glassware hanging over the bar and the city skyline filling the wide windows outside."},"sg-mys":{"txt":"This is the dining room of a Chicago lake cruise vessel, with banquet tables, a bar and a lit ceiling cove that washes the room in soft blue. The renderings show the room dressed for dinner, with places set at every table, a patterned tile wall beside the bar and the lakefront through the windows."},"sg-nor":{"txt":"This is the interior of a dining vessel, with a bar, a lounge and a dining deck. Guests can sit at the tile-fronted bar, settle into the lounge sofa or take a table along the windows. The renderings show the rooms by day and at dusk, with city lights across the water."},"sg-ody":{"txt":"Odyssey is a glass-enclosed dining vessel on the Chicago River. The glass walls and roof keep the skyline in view from every table, with a bar at one end of the dining room and an open deck with standing tables outside. The renderings place the boat on the river among the downtown towers."},"wha-120":{"txt":"This project adds upper-floor tenant amenities and a roof terrace on floors 23 and 24 of 120 South LaSalle in Chicago. An open stair beside tall windows links the two levels, leading to a lounge with a bar and game tables. Outside, the terrace offers deck seating, a planted green wall and a shade structure with the downtown skyline all around."},"wha-1sw":{"txt":"This project covers the lobby reception, tenant lounge and conference center at 1 South Wacker in Chicago. In the lobby, a long white desk carries the building name against dark stone walls. Elsewhere, a round reception desk sits under a circular wood ceiling, with lounge seating and glass-fronted meeting rooms close by."},"wha-200j":{"txt":"This is the repositioning of a Loop office building. A new glass entry and canopy mark the address at the sidewalk and open onto a brighter lobby. Tenants get a lounge with long shared tables, soft seating by the windows, a bar under a wood slat ceiling and plenty of plants."},"wha-222":{"txt":"This project reworks the entry plaza, canopy, lobby and tenant lounge at 222 South Riverside Plaza in Chicago. Steps and planted terraces lead up from the street to a lit canopy over the doors. Inside, the lobby is pale stone and glass, and the lounge gathers people around a long fireplace set in a wood wall, with a cafe counter nearby."},"wha-2pp":{"txt":"This project covers the lobby, game lounge and tenant amenities at 2 Pierce Place. A curved wall carrying the building name leads people in from the lobby. Beyond it, tenants find shuffleboard, pool and foosball tables, bright yellow window nooks and a lounge with deep sofas around a fireplace."},"wha-300w":{"txt":"These are office interiors at 300 South Wacker in Chicago, including a speculative suite. Glass-fronted conference rooms face the open office, so daylight and city views reach the desks. A cafe with bar-height and table seating gives staff a place to gather, warmed by an orange accent wall and a cluster of globe pendants."},"wha-332":{"txt":"This project renews the historic lobby at 332 South Michigan in Chicago and adds a full-floor amenities center with a fitness center, Wi-Fi lounge, elevator lobby and main stair. The lobby pairs white marble walls with its ornate gilded ceiling. On the amenities floor, tenants get a lounge with a fireplace and game tables, plus locker rooms finished in blue mosaic tile."},"wha-555":{"txt":"This is a renovation of floors 1, 2 and 17 at 555 West Monroe in Chicago, with a new lobby, cafe, conference center, fitness center and roof deck. The lobby mixes lounge seating and a cafe counter under a faceted ceiling hung with glass pendants. The fitness center looks out through full-height glass to an outdoor terrace."},"wha-701":{"txt":"This is a tenant roof deck for an office building. Shade canopies, planters, lounge seating and a bar counter turn the roof into an outdoor room for lunch and after-work events. A glass railing keeps the view open, and flowering planters and trees soften the edges."},"wha-aae":{"txt":"These are office interiors in Chicago, covering the reception, boardroom, cafe and open office. Visitors arrive at a wood and marble desk beside a slatted screen that gives a glimpse of the workspace beyond. The boardroom seats a large group at one long table with city views, and the cafe offers staff a relaxed spot with banquettes, round tables and globe pendants."},"wha-arbor":{"txt":"This is a cafe and tenant lounge for a suburban office building. A sweeping curved ceiling and a long counter organize the room, with booth, table and lounge seating beneath the exposed structure. A skyline mural runs along the back wall, and a shuffleboard table gives tenants a reason to linger."},"wha-butt":{"txt":"These are shared tenant amenities for a suburban office building. Tenants get a lounge with soft seating and games, a self-serve cafe market, and a long communal counter under the exposed structure. Yellow accent walls and warm wood furniture brighten the concrete shell, and a pool table sits at the far end of the lounge."},"wha-chee":{"txt":"These are office interiors covering the reception, open office and cafe. A wood slat ceiling runs overhead from the elevators to a green reception desk and a small seating area by the windows. Wood floors carry through to the open office, and the cafe gives staff a long island with stools for breaks and casual meetings."},"wha-chest":{"txt":"This project brings an amenity lounge, game room and shared work space to Chestnut Place. White ceiling fins float over dark wood floors and tie the rooms together. Tenants can meet in a glass-fronted conference room, play a game of pool, or settle in near the kitchen counter with a coffee."},"wha-fulc":{"txt":"This project covers the storefront entry, lobby and tenant lounge at 250 East Wisconsin. A lit canopy sign marks the entry from the sidewalk, and the white lobby is warmed by a red reception desk and red lounge chairs. The tenant lounge is a round room with a curved sofa, colorful ottomans and a cafe counter."},"wha-glen":{"txt":"This is the repositioning of an office building in Glenview, Illinois. A new glass entry pavilion leads to a skylit atrium with a reception desk, lounge seating and a cafe for tenants. Curved glass at the entry and round ceiling canopies inside soften the original building's straight lines."},"wha-henr":{"txt":"These are office and showroom interiors for a furniture dealer in Itasca, Illinois. The open office is organized by brightly colored volumes under the exposed roof structure, so the workspace doubles as a working display of the product. Glass-fronted rooms inside the red, yellow and blue volumes keep meetings visible from the desks."},"wha-hl3":{"txt":"Highland Landmark III is an office building in Downers Grove, Illinois, where the lobby, cafe and fitness center were given upgrades for the people who work there. The two-story lobby pairs wood panels with a crystal chandelier and a curved lounge group. The cafe adds a long shared table and a green banquette by the windows, and the fitness center gets a bold red patterned wall."},"wha-hsbc":{"txt":"These workplace interiors for HSBC in Arlington Heights, Illinois, cover the open office, the collaboration areas and the corridors. Long rows of shared desks sit beside glass-fronted meeting rooms, and lounge seating with a fireplace and a kitchen counter gives staff somewhere to step away from the desk. Bands of color in the carpet follow the corridors across the floor."},"wha-mac":{"txt":"These office interiors for the MacArthur Foundation include a cafe, the reception area and conference rooms. Visitors arrive at a wood reception desk beside an open stair with a black metal railing, with a ring of armchairs for waiting. The cafe sits under a warm wood ceiling with a serving counter and small tables, and the conference rooms have glass fronts that keep them open to the floor."},"wha-meade":{"txt":"These headquarters interiors for Meade Electric in Willowbrook, Illinois, cover the reception area, the open office and the cafe. Guests are met by a wood wall carrying the company name, a polished concrete floor and a row of high windows. The open office runs under the exposed roof structure with shared tables between workstations, and the cafe has a full kitchen, high tables and a banquette along the glass."},"wha-ond":{"txt":"One North Dearborn in Chicago gains a tenant amenity floor, a fitness center and a roof deck. The lounge sits under exposed red steel trusses, with sofas, a bar and booth seating for meeting or working away from the desk. Up on the roof, lounge furniture, umbrellas and planters look out to the downtown skyline, and the fitness center keeps its ducts and concrete columns in view."},"wha-ott":{"txt":"These studies look at the atrium lobby, the entry canopy and the plaza of an office tower in Oakbrook Terrace, Illinois. Outside, a curved canopy and a fountain mark the front door, and a terrace with tables and red umbrellas gives tenants a place to sit. Inside, the tall atrium is tested with two ideas, one with hanging colored cubes and one with a crystal chandelier."},"wha-ott25":{"txt":"25 Ottawa in Grand Rapids, Michigan, is a heavy-timber loft building repositioned as office space, covering the exterior, lobby, fitness center and office floors. The red brick shell and arched windows stay, with new storefronts and a patio at the sidewalk. Inside, the original timber posts and beams are left exposed, so the lobby, the gym and the open office floors all keep the warmth of the old structure."},"wha-p44":{"txt":"These interiors for Project 44 cover the open office, a lounge and a game room. The lounge gathers sofas around a planted green wall and a sparkling chandelier, right beside the desks. Concrete columns and exposed ductwork run throughout, a wall clad like a shipping container adds color, and the game room puts a ping pong table next to the kitchen island."},"wha-pfz":{"txt":"These workplace interiors for the Pfizer H1 site consolidation cover the cafe, the atrium, the open office and the break areas. A cafe counter sits in the tall concrete atrium with bright blue and yellow chairs around it, and the dining room lines a long counter along the windows. Upstairs, break areas with kitchenettes and soft seating give staff a spot to pause near their desks."},"wha-pp":{"txt":"Presidents Plaza in Chicago is an office property renovated with a new lobby, a two-story fitness center, a restaurant and bar, and a cafe. The bar opens straight off the lobby, and the lounge beyond feels like a club room, with leather sofas, bookshelves and globe chandeliers. In the fitness center, wide steps link the reception level to a turf training floor below."},"wha-river":{"txt":"These lobby and common area improvements are for an office building in Rosemont, Illinois. The schemes add a sculptural reception desk, a hanging light feature and new lounge seating to the existing two-story space. White brick walls keep the room bright, and curved benches in orange, green and blue give visitors an easy place to wait near the front desk."},"wha-sal":{"txt":"These office interiors for The Salvation Army in Hoffman Estates, Illinois, include an assembly space, a cafe lounge, the lobby and a stair. The assembly space sets rows of chairs around a low platform under a wood ceiling. In the cafe lounge, round ceiling discs float over soft seating and a red kettle mural, and the lobby stair rises beside a tall panel lettered with the mission."},"wha-shaf":{"txt":"One Shafer, at 6400 Shafer Court in Rosemont, Illinois, is a repositioning of the entry, lobby, tenant lounge and terrace. A new sign frames the revolving door at the top of the entry steps, and the two-story lobby gains a central seating group. The tenant lounge has a reclaimed wood nook and globe chandeliers, and its glass wall opens onto a terrace with a stone feature wall."},"wha-vail":{"txt":"Vail Apartments is a residential development studied through massing, elevations and unit interiors. The drawings show apartments with an attached parking structure, with stone bases, timber gables and balconies stepping along a sloped site. A massing view checks the roofline against the slope, and the bedroom rendering shows a unit with a wide window to the mountain."},"wha-warr":{"txt":"These are lobby renovation options for an office building in Lisle, Illinois. Each option keeps the view through to the entry and changes the wall finishes, seating and lighting, so the owner could compare them side by side. One wraps the wall in light wood with red swivel chairs, and another uses white stone, purple chairs and a cluster of pendant lights."},"wha-willis":{"txt":"These are speculative office suites in Willis Tower in Chicago, built out to lease ready-to-use. Each suite centers on a shared cafe and lounge under a curved ceiling, with screens and bright furniture marking places to meet. A teal wall and copper pendants anchor the kitchen island, so the cafe reads as the heart of the floor with the desks arranged around it."},"wha-windy":{"txt":"Windy Point is a suburban office building with new shared tenant amenities: a lounge, a cafe and a fitness center. The renderings show the three rooms as places tenants would use through the working day. The lounge and cafe share bright pink accent walls and a mix of soft chairs and cafe tables, and the fitness center lines its treadmills up facing the windows and trees."},"wha-wood":{"txt":"Woodland Falls is an office building in Mettawa, Illinois, with a lobby enhancement and a new tenant lounge. The two-story lobby gets a warmer entry wall and seating, and the lounge adds a cafe counter and places to work away from the desk. In the lounge, a curved sofa faces a pair of fireplaces, with a patterned ceiling panel floating over the tables."}};